1
00:00:04,780 --> 00:00:05,810
Good to see you.

2
00:00:06,280 --> 00:00:08,510
Welcome back to Steadfast Men.

3
00:00:08,980 --> 00:00:12,970
This is Lesson Four.
It's called Stop Waiting.

4
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:14,670
Here's how this goes.

5
00:00:15,260 --> 00:00:18,010
A wait that quits looking like a decision.

6
00:00:18,520 --> 00:00:21,890
The question God asked a
man who was already found.

7
00:00:22,420 --> 00:00:24,650
The nicer names a wait borrows.

8
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:27,910
Patience. Peace. Getting ready.

9
00:00:28,440 --> 00:00:29,410
Even faith.

10
00:00:29,960 --> 00:00:35,630
What the people near you learn from it,
and a man who moved three years late.

11
00:00:36,180 --> 00:00:40,250
One name, one small move,
and the noon you do it by.

12
00:00:41,300 --> 00:00:46,250
Lesson Three stayed on the last
mark, the question of who pays a man.

13
00:00:46,640 --> 00:00:48,930
The other three were
left for their own hours.

14
00:00:49,360 --> 00:00:50,930
This is the first of them.

15
00:00:51,420 --> 00:00:53,730
You met the name on a quiet Tuesday.

16
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:55,830
Today it gets the hour.

17
00:00:56,380 --> 00:00:57,690
Did you do the quiet thing?

18
00:00:58,740 --> 00:01:01,490
If you did, keep it quiet. Don't tell me.

19
00:01:02,040 --> 00:01:07,310
First time through? Jump in. The earlier
lessons are not a test you failed.

20
00:01:07,720 --> 00:01:10,990
Pull your chair in a little.
Closer than feels natural.

21
00:01:11,480 --> 00:01:14,210
You and I stay with one lesson at a time.

22
00:01:16,100 --> 00:01:19,070
I've got to start with a
confession about my garage.

23
00:01:19,440 --> 00:01:24,570
There's a stack of floor tile out there,
enough to redo our downstairs bathroom.

24
00:01:25,020 --> 00:01:27,510
I bought it on sale, forty percent off.

25
00:01:27,980 --> 00:01:32,590
It's been out there so long that nobody
in my house calls it the tile anymore.

26
00:01:32,880 --> 00:01:34,970
My wife and I call it the table.

27
00:01:35,360 --> 00:01:39,290
She sets the groceries on it.
Last month she set a lamp there.

28
00:01:39,720 --> 00:01:41,690
I think the lamp means I lost.

29
00:01:42,740 --> 00:01:46,330
That stack is a small
picture. Nothing's broken.

30
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:49,030
Nothing's lost. It's waiting on me.

31
00:01:49,620 --> 00:01:53,010
I've let it wait so long it
quit looking like a decision.

32
00:01:53,640 --> 00:01:55,330
I'd bet you've got a stack too.

33
00:01:55,760 --> 00:02:00,110
Maybe not in a garage. Maybe a
conversation you keep walking around.

34
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:05,270
When you hear passive, you
probably picture a man on a couch.

35
00:02:05,660 --> 00:02:08,390
Remote on his chest. Blinds down.

36
00:02:08,760 --> 00:02:13,830
Anyone can see him. He has the better
shot, because he knows he's on the couch.

37
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:17,590
The man I worry about
is up before the alarm.

38
00:02:17,980 --> 00:02:20,690
Good at his job. The one people call.

39
00:02:21,100 --> 00:02:25,310
Jumper cables in his truck, a
tarp, and a spare everything.

40
00:02:25,760 --> 00:02:29,930
If your car dies in a parking lot,
he's the one you want walking by.

41
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:33,910
A short list in his life
has been waiting for years.

42
00:02:34,340 --> 00:02:38,550
Not the gutters. The big ones.
The call back to the doctor.

43
00:02:38,900 --> 00:02:40,990
The apology he owes his sister.

44
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:45,790
The friend who's drinking again, and
doesn't know that this man knows.

45
00:02:47,080 --> 00:02:49,290
One of those is in your head right now.

46
00:02:49,740 --> 00:02:52,650
No details. Just notice it. Yeah.

47
00:02:53,080 --> 00:02:54,010
Hold it a second.

48
00:02:54,500 --> 00:02:57,410
That man is busy. He isn't lazy.

49
00:02:57,900 --> 00:03:01,110
You'd drive across town at
midnight for a buddy with a flat.

50
00:03:01,560 --> 00:03:02,150
Let it go.

51
00:03:02,880 --> 00:03:05,610
Busy is the best hiding place I know.

52
00:03:06,040 --> 00:03:08,130
Nobody gets in trouble for being needed.

53
00:03:08,540 --> 00:03:11,850
Busy gets you thanked.
Busy gets you a plaque.

54
00:03:12,260 --> 00:03:16,290
I've never seen a plaque for the call
a man finally makes to his brother.

55
00:03:16,880 --> 00:03:19,670
I answer work email in
about ninety seconds.

56
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:24,210
Kind of proud of that. My brother left
me a voicemail back in the spring.

57
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:26,130
I still haven't called him back.

58
00:03:26,560 --> 00:03:28,410
I've listened to it six times.

59
00:03:28,880 --> 00:03:30,770
Six times I could have called him.

60
00:03:32,640 --> 00:03:37,670
One of the first questions God ever asked
a man is in Genesis chapter three, verse

61
00:03:37,600 --> 00:03:41,850
nine. "But the Lord God called
to the man, Where are you?"

62
00:03:43,320 --> 00:03:44,310
Here's what gets me.

63
00:03:44,800 --> 00:03:49,390
God wasn't lost. He wasn't squinting
through the trees, going, Adam?

64
00:03:49,740 --> 00:03:50,150
Buddy?

65
00:03:50,700 --> 00:03:53,510
God knew exactly where
the man was standing.

66
00:03:53,820 --> 00:03:56,810
The question wasn't for
God. It was for the man.

67
00:03:57,280 --> 00:04:00,170
Notice who God called. Not the serpent.

68
00:04:00,360 --> 00:04:02,530
Not the tree. The man.

69
00:04:03,020 --> 00:04:06,670
God came looking for the one he
had put in charge of that garden.

70
00:04:07,040 --> 00:04:11,410
When something's drifting in a house,
God doesn't usually start with the kids.

71
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:16,710
You ask a question you already know so
the other person hears himself say it.

72
00:04:17,020 --> 00:04:18,610
You want the ownership.

73
00:04:19,900 --> 00:04:22,910
I do it with my kids.
Where are your shoes?

74
00:04:23,960 --> 00:04:28,210
I know where they are. They're in the
middle of the hallway, right where I'm about

75
00:04:28,100 --> 00:04:29,230
to step in the dark.

76
00:04:29,760 --> 00:04:34,850
I'm not asking for directions. I'm asking
them to walk over there and deal with it.

77
00:04:35,380 --> 00:04:38,350
That's how God comes
after a man who's parked.

78
00:04:38,860 --> 00:04:43,330
You can argue with a lecture.
A question, you have to answer.

79
00:04:43,940 --> 00:04:48,790
Quit standing behind all the good stuff,
and answer from where you actually are.

80
00:04:49,380 --> 00:04:52,230
You may be standing in a very full life.

81
00:04:52,620 --> 00:04:55,510
On one thing, you haven't moved in years.

82
00:04:56,000 --> 00:05:00,830
Not because you don't care. Moving would
cost you something, and standing still

83
00:05:00,780 --> 00:05:02,210
hasn't sent a bill yet.

84
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:04,210
God knows which thing.

85
00:05:04,720 --> 00:05:06,070
You already know it too.

86
00:05:07,920 --> 00:05:10,890
Waiting hardly ever calls itself waiting.

87
00:05:11,240 --> 00:05:15,130
It borrows a better word, something
that sounds good on a Sunday.

88
00:05:15,740 --> 00:05:18,490
Most days the word is patience.

89
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:20,250
I'm giving it time.

90
00:05:20,800 --> 00:05:24,050
Sometimes that's true. Some
things do need a minute.

91
00:05:24,340 --> 00:05:26,410
A fence post needs a minute to set.

92
00:05:27,040 --> 00:05:31,810
A lot of the time a man asks the
calendar to do a job only he can do.

93
00:05:32,360 --> 00:05:34,930
The calendar can't
apologize to your sister.

94
00:05:35,260 --> 00:05:39,690
It turns the page. Your sister is
still sitting on the other side.

95
00:05:40,700 --> 00:05:42,310
Or the word is peace.

96
00:05:42,920 --> 00:05:44,430
I don't want to stir anything up.

97
00:05:45,120 --> 00:05:50,870
The house stays calm, and a little lonely,
like a waiting room with nice magazines.

98
00:05:51,580 --> 00:05:53,850
If you're married, you know this one.

99
00:05:54,380 --> 00:05:57,450
She brought a thing up once, maybe twice.

100
00:05:58,040 --> 00:06:01,670
You nodded and said, yeah,
we should talk about that.

101
00:06:02,160 --> 00:06:03,390
Three Christmases ago.

102
00:06:04,020 --> 00:06:05,650
She hasn't brought it up since.

103
00:06:06,180 --> 00:06:07,410
It didn't get fixed.

104
00:06:07,860 --> 00:06:10,290
She figured out where
it goes when she does.

105
00:06:10,940 --> 00:06:12,390
You call that peace.

106
00:06:12,960 --> 00:06:14,490
She calls it something else.

107
00:06:15,140 --> 00:06:16,810
Settled is peace.

108
00:06:17,380 --> 00:06:18,930
Shelved is this.

109
00:06:19,980 --> 00:06:22,010
Maybe you went quiet for a reason.

110
00:06:22,620 --> 00:06:27,570
Maybe you grew up in a loud house, where
the next thing said out loud was always the

111
00:06:27,480 --> 00:06:28,430
wrong thing.

112
00:06:28,940 --> 00:06:34,450
You spoke up once, it went bad, and quiet
started to feel like the smart play.

113
00:06:35,100 --> 00:06:36,830
I'm not going to bark at you for that.

114
00:06:37,180 --> 00:06:39,790
It kept you safe once. I get that.

115
00:06:40,300 --> 00:06:45,750
If the danger is gone and the quiet
stayed, what's left is a habit with good

116
00:06:45,660 --> 00:06:46,350
manners.

117
00:06:47,400 --> 00:06:49,490
Sometimes the word is humility.

118
00:06:50,040 --> 00:06:51,390
Who am I to bring it up?

119
00:06:52,460 --> 00:06:55,670
I'm not the expert. Somebody
else is closer to it.

120
00:06:56,140 --> 00:06:58,370
You're her husband. That's who.

121
00:06:58,920 --> 00:07:01,910
You're his dad. You're the one who saw it.

122
00:07:02,360 --> 00:07:04,870
If you saw it, you're already in it.

123
00:07:05,960 --> 00:07:08,430
Sometimes the word is getting ready.

124
00:07:09,060 --> 00:07:10,650
This one is mine.

125
00:07:11,260 --> 00:07:14,070
I researched kayaks for about two years.

126
00:07:14,440 --> 00:07:16,930
Read the reviews. Watched the videos.

127
00:07:17,300 --> 00:07:20,570
Knew the weight of every
model down to the ounce.

128
00:07:21,240 --> 00:07:26,770
I own zero kayaks. I have never been
more prepared to not be on a lake.

129
00:07:27,320 --> 00:07:28,970
I could tell you which paddle to buy.

130
00:07:29,400 --> 00:07:31,850
I just couldn't tell you
what the water feels like.

131
00:07:32,480 --> 00:07:36,410
A man can get really good at
studying a thing he never does.

132
00:07:36,880 --> 00:07:39,750
Kayaks can take that. A marriage can't.

133
00:07:40,060 --> 00:07:43,190
A kid can't. The friend
who's drinking can't.

134
00:07:43,820 --> 00:07:48,490
I've known a man who read three books on
being a dad and hasn't asked his kid a real

135
00:07:48,380 --> 00:07:49,950
question since spring.

136
00:07:50,560 --> 00:07:52,430
Some people do the same with church.

137
00:07:52,840 --> 00:07:55,790
They're going to come back.
They're looking at a few places.

138
00:07:56,200 --> 00:07:58,150
They've been looking for three years.

139
00:07:59,200 --> 00:08:02,690
If you're young, or you're
single, there's a special version.

140
00:08:03,120 --> 00:08:05,330
It sounds like, once I.

141
00:08:06,080 --> 00:08:09,370
Once I get the better job.
Once I find the right girl.

142
00:08:09,860 --> 00:08:11,570
Once I've got a little money saved.

143
00:08:11,980 --> 00:08:13,610
Once I've got my head on straight.

144
00:08:14,220 --> 00:08:17,390
Somehow that sentence never
gets to the second half.

145
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:22,510
Nobody is coming with a permission slip
that says you can start your own life now.

146
00:08:22,900 --> 00:08:24,670
You started it a while ago.

147
00:08:25,280 --> 00:08:30,170
The man you'll be in ten years is getting
built right now, on the days you keep

148
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:33,030
calling practice. It's already running.

149
00:08:34,860 --> 00:08:37,770
Then there's the one with
the best excuse of all.

150
00:08:38,360 --> 00:08:38,910
Faith.

151
00:08:39,640 --> 00:08:40,850
I'm waiting on the Lord.

152
00:08:41,460 --> 00:08:45,250
Scripture says to wait on the Lord,
and I won't take that from you.

153
00:08:45,600 --> 00:08:47,070
It's all over the Psalms.

154
00:08:47,600 --> 00:08:50,170
Maybe you honestly don't
know the next step.

155
00:08:50,560 --> 00:08:51,310
That's real.

156
00:08:51,880 --> 00:08:54,010
Ask the Lord. Ask a brother.

157
00:08:54,520 --> 00:08:56,510
Stay on your feet while you ask.

158
00:08:57,180 --> 00:08:58,350
There's another kind.

159
00:08:58,820 --> 00:09:04,050
The next step is sitting right there,
and a man pins God's name on the delay.

160
00:09:04,520 --> 00:09:06,930
That's a heavy name to pin on something.

161
00:09:07,300 --> 00:09:08,490
God never signed it.

162
00:09:09,540 --> 00:09:12,790
Joshua chapter eighteen, verse three.

163
00:09:12,640 --> 00:09:17,910
"So Joshua said to the Israelites: How
long will you wait before you begin to take

164
00:09:17,800 --> 00:09:22,550
possession of the land that the Lord, the
God of your ancestors, has given you?"

165
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:26,650
Hear that last part. Has given you.

166
00:09:27,100 --> 00:09:30,750
The land was already theirs.
God had done his part.

167
00:09:31,060 --> 00:09:34,010
The promising part. The going-ahead part.

168
00:09:34,300 --> 00:09:38,210
All of it. They were camped
out, waiting to feel like it.

169
00:09:38,560 --> 00:09:40,410
They were waiting on themselves.

170
00:09:41,520 --> 00:09:44,170
Here's a test. You can do it in the truck.

171
00:09:44,740 --> 00:09:50,030
When you say you're waiting on God, ask
whether some piece of it already has your

172
00:09:49,940 --> 00:09:50,690
name on it.

173
00:09:51,200 --> 00:09:55,270
If it does, do that piece.
The piece you can see.

174
00:09:55,740 --> 00:09:56,870
Not the whole map.

175
00:09:57,480 --> 00:10:01,530
You can trust God for the rain and
still put the seed in the ground.

176
00:10:02,260 --> 00:10:04,350
Ask yourself Joshua's question.

177
00:10:04,780 --> 00:10:05,870
How long.

178
00:10:06,380 --> 00:10:08,450
Not a mood. A number.

179
00:10:08,980 --> 00:10:10,770
Months. Years.

180
00:10:11,480 --> 00:10:14,550
I did this with the tile. Eleven months.

181
00:10:14,940 --> 00:10:18,190
For tile. A thing I could
have finished in a day.

182
00:10:18,720 --> 00:10:21,050
I had to go dig up the order confirmation.

183
00:10:21,620 --> 00:10:25,770
Be honest. Rounding down is
just one more way to wait.

184
00:10:27,620 --> 00:10:32,290
The people near you learn your wait,
even if you never say a word about it.

185
00:10:32,900 --> 00:10:35,510
My daughter asked me to
put a shelf up in her room.

186
00:10:35,960 --> 00:10:39,010
Simple job. Two brackets, one board.

187
00:10:39,480 --> 00:10:41,910
I've hung heavier things with worse tools.

188
00:10:42,540 --> 00:10:44,290
I said, Saturday, kiddo.

189
00:10:45,100 --> 00:10:47,150
I said it a few Saturdays in a row.

190
00:10:47,620 --> 00:10:48,510
More than a few.

191
00:10:49,280 --> 00:10:52,250
One morning my phone
buzzes, middle of a meeting.

192
00:10:52,580 --> 00:10:55,310
A calendar invite, from my own kid.

193
00:10:55,840 --> 00:11:00,870
Subject line. Dad, the shelf.
Saturday, ten in the morning.

194
00:11:01,320 --> 00:11:04,410
She even set a reminder,
fifteen minutes before.

195
00:11:05,080 --> 00:11:07,230
I laughed, and then I didn't.

196
00:11:07,780 --> 00:11:12,710
She is twelve years old, and she had
already figured out that asking me wasn't

197
00:11:12,580 --> 00:11:14,870
enough. She had to manage me.

198
00:11:15,380 --> 00:11:17,490
She's better at it than my boss.

199
00:11:18,660 --> 00:11:22,990
They start guessing about the man
who won't move, and they stay quiet.

200
00:11:23,500 --> 00:11:24,330
Is he mad?

201
00:11:25,380 --> 00:11:26,350
Is he tired?

202
00:11:27,400 --> 00:11:29,070
Does he even care about this?

203
00:11:30,120 --> 00:11:31,270
That man was me.

204
00:11:32,080 --> 00:11:33,030
I did care.

205
00:11:33,560 --> 00:11:35,090
I cared from a distance.

206
00:11:35,800 --> 00:11:41,130
After a while the guessing stops, and a
life gets built around the hole where you

207
00:11:41,140 --> 00:11:41,670
should be.

208
00:11:42,300 --> 00:11:46,350
Kids do it. Wives do it.
Friends do it fastest.

209
00:11:46,780 --> 00:11:51,030
A friend who can't reach you stops
trying and calls it being busy too.

210
00:11:51,680 --> 00:11:54,870
I put the shelf up that
Saturday, ten in the morning.

211
00:11:55,260 --> 00:12:00,250
She stood in the doorway the whole time,
handing me screws like a surgical nurse.

212
00:12:00,660 --> 00:12:02,030
It took twenty minutes.

213
00:12:02,500 --> 00:12:03,990
Twenty minutes.

214
00:12:04,460 --> 00:12:06,310
She didn't need a shelf that bad.

215
00:12:06,700 --> 00:12:10,010
She needed to know that
when she asked, I'd move.

216
00:12:10,520 --> 00:12:12,570
I'd been protecting that for a month.

217
00:12:14,440 --> 00:12:18,950
A man I'll call Curtis coached youth
baseball for close to twenty years.

218
00:12:19,400 --> 00:12:23,630
If you had a kid in that town, Curtis
probably taught him to quit flinching at a

219
00:12:23,560 --> 00:12:24,370
fastball.

220
00:12:24,840 --> 00:12:26,870
Good man. Honest man.

221
00:12:27,380 --> 00:12:30,610
Every practice, a bucket
of balls and a thermos.

222
00:12:31,260 --> 00:12:35,370
A few years before I met him, his wife
asked if they could see a counselor.

223
00:12:35,840 --> 00:12:39,710
Nothing was on fire. She felt
like they'd turned into roommates.

224
00:12:40,080 --> 00:12:41,090
Nice roommates.

225
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:45,050
Curtis said sure, after the
season, and he meant it.

226
00:12:45,480 --> 00:12:49,430
Then fall ball. Then a
travel team needed a coach.

227
00:12:49,860 --> 00:12:51,430
Then spring came back.

228
00:12:51,940 --> 00:12:55,890
Every time she asked, the
kids needed him, and they did.

229
00:12:56,360 --> 00:13:00,650
The worst day wasn't a fight.
It was the day she quit asking.

230
00:13:01,020 --> 00:13:04,610
He came home and she had moved
her things into the guest room.

231
00:13:05,060 --> 00:13:06,850
No yelling. She said,

232
00:13:07,340 --> 00:13:10,050
I'm tired of waiting on
the season to be over.

233
00:13:11,380 --> 00:13:13,450
Curtis sat on it two days.

234
00:13:13,920 --> 00:13:19,290
He told me he kept waiting to feel ready,
for a morning he'd wake up knowing exactly

235
00:13:19,200 --> 00:13:20,010
what to say.

236
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:22,110
That morning never showed up.

237
00:13:22,600 --> 00:13:23,690
A Thursday did.

238
00:13:24,180 --> 00:13:29,050
He got to the field early, sat in the
dugout, phone in his hand, ball bag at his

239
00:13:28,980 --> 00:13:31,290
feet, and called the counselor's office.

240
00:13:31,760 --> 00:13:35,890
His hands were sweating so bad he
almost dropped the phone in the dirt.

241
00:13:36,460 --> 00:13:39,010
The lady said, we've got Monday at four.

242
00:13:39,460 --> 00:13:41,770
Curtis said, I've got practice.

243
00:13:42,280 --> 00:13:44,350
Then he heard himself. He said,

244
00:13:44,880 --> 00:13:46,210
no. We'll be there.

245
00:13:46,760 --> 00:13:49,450
He told his wife that
night. She didn't cry.

246
00:13:49,780 --> 00:13:52,310
She didn't hug him. She said okay.

247
00:13:52,980 --> 00:13:56,570
The first appointment
was, his word, awful.

248
00:13:57,180 --> 00:14:02,110
Long silences. Curtis said he'd
rather take a line drive off the shin.

249
00:14:02,620 --> 00:14:05,250
They went back, and they kept going back.

250
00:14:05,760 --> 00:14:08,770
About a year in, she said
something he wrote down.

251
00:14:09,140 --> 00:14:09,730
She said,

252
00:14:10,260 --> 00:14:12,570
I quit waiting on you a long time ago.

253
00:14:13,060 --> 00:14:14,450
I'm glad you came anyway.

254
00:14:15,800 --> 00:14:20,070
Curtis wasn't short on love.
He was short on the first move.

255
00:14:20,500 --> 00:14:23,210
He had been calling that
shortage by a nice name.

256
00:14:23,580 --> 00:14:24,930
The kids need me.

257
00:14:25,580 --> 00:14:29,330
He waited to feel ready,
and ready never came first.

258
00:14:29,660 --> 00:14:30,370
It doesn't.

259
00:14:30,820 --> 00:14:34,750
Ready shows up after you
move. Usually a while after.

260
00:14:35,100 --> 00:14:36,710
Sometimes a year after.

261
00:14:37,200 --> 00:14:41,090
Late still counted. If
you feel late, hear that.

262
00:14:41,500 --> 00:14:45,590
Curtis made that call three years
behind, and it still mattered.

263
00:14:45,920 --> 00:14:51,370
The call took four minutes. Three years
of waiting, and the move itself was four

264
00:14:51,300 --> 00:14:52,990
minutes on a dugout bench.

265
00:14:53,480 --> 00:14:55,590
Most of what you're
waiting on is like that.

266
00:14:55,900 --> 00:14:59,670
The dread is huge. The move is small.

267
00:15:00,100 --> 00:15:00,990
Lopsided.

268
00:15:01,500 --> 00:15:04,690
A man measures the dread,
and skips the move.

269
00:15:06,560 --> 00:15:09,570
James doesn't give you a
soft place to land on this.

270
00:15:09,960 --> 00:15:12,630
The seventeenth verse
of James chapter four.

271
00:15:13,240 --> 00:15:17,770
"If anyone, then, knows the good
they ought to do and doesn't do it,

272
00:15:18,220 --> 00:15:19,530
it is sin for them."

273
00:15:20,980 --> 00:15:23,770
Hard verse. It takes the middle away.

274
00:15:24,240 --> 00:15:29,070
A man likes a middle, where he skips the
wrong thing, skips the right thing, and

275
00:15:28,980 --> 00:15:29,650
holds.

276
00:15:30,160 --> 00:15:35,710
James says there isn't one. If you know it
and you're sitting on it, God has a word

277
00:15:35,620 --> 00:15:38,010
for that. The word isn't careful.

278
00:15:38,740 --> 00:15:41,690
Name the thing small enough
that a morning could hold it.

279
00:15:42,060 --> 00:15:44,810
Your whole marriage is
too big for a Thursday.

280
00:15:45,200 --> 00:15:47,010
A four-minute phone call can fit.

281
00:15:47,460 --> 00:15:51,070
Find the smallest move
that is still a real move.

282
00:15:51,520 --> 00:15:53,250
Finding the number doesn't count.

283
00:15:53,580 --> 00:15:54,670
The call does.

284
00:15:55,160 --> 00:16:00,550
Do it before noon. By about three in the
afternoon, my excuses have had all day to

285
00:16:00,440 --> 00:16:02,730
get dressed, and they sound responsible.

286
00:16:03,220 --> 00:16:05,530
You've practiced waiting for years.

287
00:16:05,940 --> 00:16:08,990
The first real move will
feel like you cut in line.

288
00:16:09,300 --> 00:16:11,930
You didn't. You finally took your turn.

289
00:16:13,760 --> 00:16:16,870
The same wait shows up
in every kind of house.

290
00:16:17,180 --> 00:16:18,910
It changes its name at the door.

291
00:16:19,400 --> 00:16:22,330
In a young man's apartment,
it's called someday.

292
00:16:22,800 --> 00:16:25,570
Someday stays busy. He's never home.

293
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:29,290
With a new baby, it's called
when things settle down.

294
00:16:29,680 --> 00:16:31,190
They won't. I checked.

295
00:16:31,660 --> 00:16:36,450
With a big career, it's called next quarter,
and next quarter has a next quarter.

296
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:40,850
For the man worn out at church,
it's called let somebody else.

297
00:16:41,240 --> 00:16:45,070
There's always a somebody else,
until one day there isn't.

298
00:16:45,640 --> 00:16:49,030
After a divorce, it's called
when I'm not so angry.

299
00:16:49,600 --> 00:16:52,250
You might wait a long time
to feel fair about it.

300
00:16:52,620 --> 00:16:54,550
If you're hurting, go slow.

301
00:16:55,180 --> 00:16:57,350
One small true thing is plenty.

302
00:16:57,840 --> 00:16:59,530
A text. A coffee.

303
00:17:00,020 --> 00:17:02,690
Frozen and healed are
two different things.

304
00:17:03,020 --> 00:17:04,870
You don't have to thaw all at once.

305
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:09,230
If you're older, it's
called nobody asked me.

306
00:17:09,880 --> 00:17:12,450
The job's done. The kids are grown.

307
00:17:12,920 --> 00:17:15,570
You're waiting on somebody
to invite you to matter.

308
00:17:15,920 --> 00:17:19,430
That invite is not
coming. You still matter.

309
00:17:19,900 --> 00:17:21,450
People don't think to ask.

310
00:17:21,900 --> 00:17:25,170
A younger man doesn't know
how to knock, so go find one.

311
00:17:25,580 --> 00:17:29,150
Ask him how he's actually
doing, and stay for the answer.

312
00:17:29,900 --> 00:17:33,670
I know a man in his seventies who
got tired of waiting to be asked.

313
00:17:34,020 --> 00:17:36,810
He started showing up early
to set out the chairs.

314
00:17:37,240 --> 00:17:40,990
Within a month, three younger
ones were showing up early too.

315
00:17:41,460 --> 00:17:43,010
They didn't come for the chairs.

316
00:17:43,400 --> 00:17:45,570
Different houses. Same wait.

317
00:17:46,200 --> 00:17:51,130
Your Father is the only one in the house
allowed to wait on you, and he has been

318
00:17:51,080 --> 00:17:53,690
more patient than you or I deserve.

319
00:17:55,520 --> 00:17:58,650
If you hold on to one
thing, hold on to this.

320
00:17:59,260 --> 00:18:02,330
Waiting almost always wears a nicer name.

321
00:18:02,740 --> 00:18:06,710
Patience. Peace. Humility. Getting ready.

322
00:18:07,240 --> 00:18:08,130
Even faith.

323
00:18:08,700 --> 00:18:13,490
Under the nice name is something you already
know is yours, and you haven't touched

324
00:18:13,400 --> 00:18:15,830
it. You could find it with the lights off.

325
00:18:16,540 --> 00:18:17,430
Four marks.

326
00:18:17,980 --> 00:18:20,310
A man who won't let his life idle.

327
00:18:20,720 --> 00:18:23,030
A man who shoulders his own load.

328
00:18:23,500 --> 00:18:27,410
A man who walks into the hard
thing ahead of the people he loves.

329
00:18:27,860 --> 00:18:30,510
A man content to be paid by God.

330
00:18:30,960 --> 00:18:35,350
Today was the first. A
steadfast man stops waiting.

331
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:39,490
The other three get stuck behind this one.

332
00:18:40,600 --> 00:18:42,050
Leave the guilt here.

333
00:18:42,660 --> 00:18:45,770
Guilt is heavy, and it
doesn't move anything.

334
00:18:46,240 --> 00:18:47,750
It just sits there with you.

335
00:18:48,480 --> 00:18:51,470
Walk out with one name and one move.

336
00:18:51,920 --> 00:18:54,630
Small enough to do the
minute you walk out.

337
00:18:55,140 --> 00:18:56,650
You don't need a new you.

338
00:18:57,240 --> 00:19:00,130
You need one thing you quit walking past.

339
00:19:00,800 --> 00:19:03,350
The tile comes off the
table this Saturday.

340
00:19:04,020 --> 00:19:07,250
My wife has heard that
before. More than once.

341
00:19:07,800 --> 00:19:09,250
So now you've heard it too.

342
00:19:10,300 --> 00:19:13,550
Let me pray, and then the
rest of this is yours.

343
00:19:14,300 --> 00:19:14,850
Father,

344
00:19:15,400 --> 00:19:18,330
you heard the name the man
in front of me is holding.

345
00:19:18,940 --> 00:19:20,290
You know how long.

346
00:19:20,940 --> 00:19:24,550
The wait has gone on so long
it feels like furniture.

347
00:19:25,180 --> 00:19:27,350
Give him four minutes of courage.

348
00:19:27,800 --> 00:19:30,030
On a real day, before lunch.

349
00:19:30,620 --> 00:19:35,690
Give him the first move before he feels
ready, and meet him on the other side of it.

350
00:19:36,240 --> 00:19:40,990
If he isn't sure about you yet, be patient
with him the way you've been patient with

351
00:19:40,900 --> 00:19:41,150
me.

352
00:19:41,860 --> 00:19:44,390
Let him see you're worth moving toward.

353
00:19:45,020 --> 00:19:45,570
Amen.

354
00:19:46,880 --> 00:19:49,090
Turn in the workbook to Lesson Four.

355
00:19:49,580 --> 00:19:50,530
Write it messy.

356
00:19:51,080 --> 00:19:52,070
Write it true.

357
00:19:52,700 --> 00:19:55,470
Three questions. Stop and write.

358
00:19:56,080 --> 00:19:56,730
First.

359
00:19:57,400 --> 00:20:00,870
What's the one thing you've been
going to get to the longest?

360
00:20:01,960 --> 00:20:06,950
Put a number on how long. Whatever's
true, not whatever sounds better.

361
00:20:09,300 --> 00:20:09,890
Second.

362
00:20:10,440 --> 00:20:13,290
Who's guessing right now,
because you won't move?

363
00:20:14,340 --> 00:20:16,830
Say the name. Not the whole story.

364
00:20:17,160 --> 00:20:18,250
Just the name.

365
00:20:20,600 --> 00:20:21,170
Third.

366
00:20:21,800 --> 00:20:25,910
What's the smallest real move
you can make on it before noon?

367
00:20:26,960 --> 00:20:30,170
Not the whole conversation.
The first sentence.

368
00:20:30,500 --> 00:20:31,650
The first call.

369
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:36,830
If a man tells you his
number, don't flinch.

370
00:20:37,160 --> 00:20:40,050
Don't fix it. Don't top it with your own.

371
00:20:40,500 --> 00:20:44,670
He just did the hard part. You
don't have to agree it's a big deal.

372
00:20:45,060 --> 00:20:46,550
You just have to hear it.

373
00:20:47,120 --> 00:20:48,770
So here's your one move.

374
00:20:49,440 --> 00:20:49,850
One.

375
00:20:50,420 --> 00:20:53,870
Text one man the move, and
ask him to check on you.

376
00:20:54,360 --> 00:20:56,650
Do it before you pull
out of the parking lot.

377
00:20:57,020 --> 00:21:00,470
The drive home is where a good
intention goes to take a nap.

378
00:21:01,540 --> 00:21:04,130
Copy one line in your own hand.

379
00:21:04,600 --> 00:21:07,250
God already asked it. Where are you?

380
00:21:07,840 --> 00:21:09,050
He already knows.

381
00:21:09,540 --> 00:21:10,970
Answer Him on your feet.

382
00:21:11,520 --> 00:21:15,090
Write it once. Put it where
you'll see it before noon.

383
00:21:15,440 --> 00:21:19,850
The bathroom mirror works. Unless your
bathroom is still waiting on tile.

384
00:21:20,320 --> 00:21:23,990
I'm done talking. Next lesson
we look at what you carry.

385
00:21:24,520 --> 00:21:25,550
Pick Up the Weight.

386
00:21:26,020 --> 00:21:28,730
Quit walking past the
thing with your name on it.

387
00:21:29,040 --> 00:21:30,850
Go make the small move.

